<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stephen of Perm</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1340–<a href="/years/1396">1396</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Saint Stephen of Perm</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stephen of Perm was a Russian missionary monk from Ustyug who converted many of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/komi-peoples">Komi</a> people to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> from 1379 and became the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Perm in 1383. He created the Old Permic alphabet for the Komi language and translated liturgical texts into it. He is venerated as a saint of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-orthodox-church">Russian Orthodox Church</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stephen-of-perm.jpg" alt="Stephen of Perm" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Лицевое житие преподобного Сергия Радонежского · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bishop_Stefan_of_Perm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the late 14th century <b>Saint Stephen of Perm</b> converted many of the Komi and created the Old Permic alphabet for their language.</blockquote><a href="/state/great-perm">Great Perm</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veliky-ustyug">Veliky Ustyug</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=60.76,46.3&amp;year=1376" aria-label="Veliky Ustyug on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5512 134 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Stephen of Perm"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5962 404h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5962 404h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=60.76,46.3&amp;year=1376">What was here in 1376? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
